From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] a refused allocation skips the operation and is counted instead of losing the device every session shares

Direct3D 11 UpdateSubresource, the initializers, buffer invalidation, image
relocation and the scratch buffers marked the whole device lost when memory ran
out, which faults every session on the shared host device. They now count the
refusal; dxvk_take_out_of_memory returns and clears the count so the embedder
faults only the session that was running.
---
